 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "The black-box convex function is modelled as F(x) = max over lines [slope, intercept] of slope * x + intercept (always convex). The candidate points are the grid x_j = a + j * eps for j = 0, 1, ... with x_j <= b. Return the smallest grid point at which F is minimal over the grid; such a point lies within eps of a true minimiser of F on [a, b]. All quantities are integers.",
